If an element given to `layout_column_wrap()` has a set `width` that's greater than the allocated column width, that column is allowed to grow, throwing off the alignment of the remaining items in the row.

In the example below, the two elements should have equal widths that share the full row width.

```r
set.seed(1234)

page_fixed(
  div(class = "my-5"),
  layout_column_wrap(
    width = 1 / 2,
    div(
      class = "border border-danger",
      style = css(width = "400px", max_width = "100%"),
      lorem::ipsum(1, 1)
    ),
    div(
      class = "border border-primary",
      lorem::ipsum(1, 1)
    )
  ) |>
  tagAppendAttributes(
    class = "p-2 border border-secondary"
  )
)
```

![image](https://github.com/rstudio/bslib/assets/5420529/f2bc1ae4-76ec-4dd6-922e-a78f253199e1)

The fix is to use `minmax(0, 1fr)`:

```patch
- grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
+ grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
```

```r
set.seed(1234)

page_fixed(
  div(class = "my-5"),
  layout_column_wrap(
    width = 1 / 2,
    div(
      class = "border border-danger",
      style = css(width = "400px", max_width = "100%"),
      lorem::ipsum(1, 1)
    ),
    div(
      class = "border border-primary",
      lorem::ipsum(1, 1)
    )
  ) |>
  tagAppendAttributes(
    class = "p-2 border border-secondary",
    style = css("grid-template-columns" = "repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr))")
  )
)
```

